    },
    {
      "entryId": "amo-3-7",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Surely the Lord GOD will do nothing, but He revealeth His secret unto His servants the prophets. In every critical transition of salvation history (the Flood, Exodus, First Advent, and the End Times), God guides and protects His covenant people through the prophetic gift. First principle: prophecy is God's chosen method of covenant warning and instruction.",
      "density": 2.9429,
      "words": 56,
      "sentences": 3,
      "maxSentenceWords": 27,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "amo-4-13",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The Creator declares man's thought, treads earth's high places. First principle: the doxological refrains of Amos arm the judgment — the God who forms and reveals is the God who punishing comes.",
      "density": 2.1143,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 23,
